course: dictionary
lesson: 7615
title: Plants in the garden
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You do not need to know every word to understand a text. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they give clues. «Stick insects rock like twigs in the wind so hunters ignore them, they eat leaves such as bramble or privet.» Stick insects eat leaves, and bramble is a plant, so privet must be a plant too.
explain: Look for more clues. The sentence says privet is a plant that stick insects eat, so it is something that grows. Privet is a bush with small, dark green, shiny leaves. Try your meaning in the sentence: «they eat leaves such as bramble or a bush with shiny leaves» still makes sense, so you have probably got it.
explain: Privet is an everyday word in Britain, Ireland and Australia, where privet hedges line front gardens. Some people know it from Harry Potter, where the Dursleys live at Privet Drive. A dictionary helps you check the exact meaning when context does not settle it.
fact: Privet is a bush with small, dark green, shiny leaves.
fact: Privet is often grown as a garden hedge.
fact: Privet flowers attract bees, so they are useful to insects.
fact: Birds eat privet berries, but the berries are poisonous to people, so never eat them.
fact: Privet Drive is the street where the Dursleys live in the Harry Potter books.
exercise: «Stick insects ... eat leaves such as bramble or privet.» What is privet? | A small animal that hunts insects | *A bush with small, dark green, shiny leaves | A bird that eats berries | A type of stick insect
exercise: Where would you most likely see a privet hedge? | Inside a fish tank | *Lining the front of a garden | On top of a mountain peak | Deep under the sea
exercise: Which statement about privet berries is true? | They are sweet and safe for people to eat | They glow in the dark | *They are poisonous to people | They are used to make bread
test: In Harry Potter, the Dursleys live on Privet ___. | Avenue | Lane | Close | *Drive
test: Which sentence uses privet correctly? | The privet swam across the pond. | She privet the cake loudly. | Privet is a kind of fish. | *The privet hedge grew tall along the path.
exam: Bees love privet flowers, but its berries can harm people. What does this tell you about privet? | It only grows in Harry Potter books | It is a kind of bird | *It is a plant useful to insects, but its berries can harm people | It is a bush that is safe to eat
